ile` does not round-trip. The terminal-safety reason holds; the \"unchanged\" claim does not.\n- **The summary overstates `versions` (read).** It says \"versions no longer prints raw note text\". `--show` still prints the raw note, now run through `plain()`. Only the listing is bounded and cleaned.\n\n**2. Missing risks**\n\n- **A refused gloss still fails a range `review` (read).** `src/commands/review.ts:86` calls `shas.map((sha) => loadGloss(sha))`, which throws for a too-big or malformed note. `git gloss review <range>` therefore still fails the whole range on one hostile note, although the change makes `show` and `html` skip it. `src/commands/why.ts:26` and `lint.ts` also use the throwing `loadGloss`. The author's \"task\" claim is scoped to show/html, so this is a gap rather than a false statement, but it is the same bug class and the docs do not mention it. Not run.\n- **Oversized notes are inconsistent across commands (read).** The docs say a refused note is skipped in a range, but `review` and `why` will abort instead. The TODO should list them.\n- **Stdin EAGAIN in `add` (read).** The author's TODO notes that `readFileSync(0)` failed on an 8 MB pipe. Since the change adds an 8 MiB limit, a user piping a near-cap note hits this failure. The risk is listed, but the TODO says \"not looked into further\" on a path the change makes more likely to matter.\n\n**3. Checked and consistent (read)**\n\n- `loadGlossInRange` rethrows `GitError`, so git failures and timeouts still fail the range, as the author says.\n- The page applies `plain()` to subject, author, date, merge subjects and decision fields. Gloss text is already cleaned by `cleanStrings` in `git.ts`, and review text by `reviews.ts:128`, so the \"already cleaned\" note holds.\n- The `--restore` path validates with `parseNote` before writing in both branches. The wip branch now uses the parsed, cleaned note rather than raw JSON. This is a behaviour change, but it is an improvement and is not called out.\n- Test changes: 20,000 items still exceed `MAX_ITEMS` (500), so the item-cap test still exercises the cap.\n\n**4. Not verified**\n\n- `git gloss lint` was not run.\n- The full suite was not run, per the rules. The orchestrator's timing failures in `test/arysync.test.ts` are outside this change's scope and were not re-run.\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
