77c3e6427cdcce","ff27c454f663da75","ff7453babd8f3fd3","ffa9047c055369f5","ffee7293cc69efe0","fff24b40c366d1a6"],"groups":["1859f7c746aff2ee","9070a1c1bea9b82d","25bdadb13dfd73d0","1020113b5a442144","f8531d5a764f45ce","9f08003b290f8c12","f433705995dbf289","fd757566acff8579","a6acfa6c03a83647","982e8fcee62dc1dc","3f85ff31636cfd5f","0b9d2802b123b950","011be64d76d9d670","fff8af07fc755ae5","6416c8e8d00d4e5b"],"findings":"**Mismatches**\n\n1. **`refusedWarning` wording reads badly (verified).** I ran `git gloss show` over a range with a note of `not json`. stderr was `warning: skipping the gloss on 191cc438d3: is not valid JSON; replace it with git gloss add --force`. The `replace(/^the gloss on \\S+ /, '')` in `src/loader.ts` strips the subject, so the message reads \"on <sha>: is not valid JSON\". The author's intent is a clear skip warning, and the output is grammatically off. Group `range-skip`. The tests only match `refused|malformed`, so they would not catch it.\n\n2. **Misplaced comment in `src/schema.ts` (read).** The new line \"A gloss note's total size, read or written…\" sits between the existing `MAX_GROUPS` comment block and `export const MAX_GROUPS = 500`. It describes `MAX_NOTE_BYTES`, which has no comment of its own and is declared after `MAX_GROUPS`. Group `note-cap`.\n\n3. **\"Refused fast\" is not what the test checks (read).** The author's evidence names the test \"a gloss note over the size cap is refused fast\". That test asserts only `within(..., 20_000)` and checks the message. The 8 MiB check also runs after the whole blob has been read (`rawNote` reads it, then `parseNote` checks size). That is accurate for \"refused before parsing\", but \"fast\" is not measured. Group `note-cap`, read.\n\n**Misgrading**: skipped per the brief.\n\n**Missing risks**\n\n4. **`versions --show` and `--restore` read the whole blob before any size check (read).** `summary` checks `cat-file -s` first, but `--show` calls `git cat-file blob` and passes the full output to `plain()`. `--restore` reads `text` in full and only then runs `parseNote`. A large blob from history is therefore loaded and cleaned in full on each of these paths, and `--show` has no size bound. The author's TODO covers the 256 MB git `maxBuffer` case but not this one. Groups `versions-clean`, `note-cap`.\n\n5. **`--restore` error rewriting depends on message text (read).** `err.message.replace(/; (replace it|re-gloss it|upgrade).*$/, '')` and `replace(/^the gloss on \\S+ is refused: /, '')` strip phrases from messages produced in another module. Rewording the message in `parseNote` or `loadGlossOf` silently changes what `--restore` prints. Group `versions-clean`.\n\n**Checks that hold**\n\n- I ran `test/hardnotes.test.ts` alone: 27 tests, 27 pass, 0 fail (verified). That covers the range skip, size cap, html strip, adopt, carry, versions, `--restore` claims refusal, review/why skip, and the 7 MiB slow-writer stdin test.\n- The html page strips invisible characters and `plain()` takes a `multiline` flag, so `--show` uses it correctly (read).\n- The README and TODO edits agree with the code: the decisions section now says the terminal-only cleaning, and the html \"applies none of this\" line is gone (read).\n- Author claims about `lint` staying single-commit are consistent with the code (read; the test asserts a clean error).\n\nVERDICT: ISSUES","verdict":"issues"}
